# ML experiments

- Inside `mlflow.start_run()`, log params, validation metrics (log loss, Brier, accuracy, AUC), and the git SHA (`git_commit` tag).
- Model selection uses validation only. Do not read test (2025) metrics to pick a model.
- Compare every candidate to the configured reference. Phase 1's default reference is the home-prior baseline (`baseline-home`: constant probability equal to the training home win rate). Phase 2 H1 and H2 compare to logistic feature set `current`. Phase 2 H3 compares to logistic feature set `h2_full`.
- Phase 1 (`python -m src.train.train --cv`) is rolling-origin CV on seasons 2016-2023. 2024 stays the final validation. 2025 is not scored. The paired comparison is log loss against the home prior.
- Phase 2 H1 (`python -m src.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis h1`) uses the same window and scores logistic `current`, `diff`, and `diff_only`, plus the home prior, Elo, and the market. Tags are `phase=2` and `hypothesis=h1-diff`. The report is `reports/phase2/`.
- Phase 2 H2 uses the same window and scores logistic `current`, `h2_def`, and `h2_full`, plus the same baselines, against logistic `current`. Tags are `phase=2` and `hypothesis=h2-season-def-regression`. The report is `reports/phase2_h2/`.
- Phase 2 H3 uses the same window and scores logistic `h2_full`, `h3_split`, and `h3_replace`, plus the same baselines, against logistic `h2_full`. Tags are `phase=2` and `hypothesis=h3-pass-rush-epa`. The report is `reports/phase2_h3/`. Reproduce it with `python -m src.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis h3`.
- Phase 2 H3 is rejected. CV 2016-2023, n=2191, logistic `h2_full` log loss 0.6377. `h3_split` 0.6393 (difference +0.0016, 95% interval -0.0009 to 0.0039) and `h3_replace` 0.6395 (difference +0.0018, 95% interval -0.0008 to 0.0043). Both have lower AUC (0.6801 and 0.6796) and lower accuracy. The splits add noise at about 270 games per season. Combined EPA already carries the signal. Recorded in `docs/experiments/phase2_h3_pass_rush_epa.md`.
- Phase 2 ridge reference (`make train-cv`) is setup work on the same window. It scores logistic `h2_full` (the reference), `logistic_l2` on `h2_full`, `h3_split`, and `h3_replace`, plus the same baselines. `logistic_l2` is L2 logistic regression whose C is chosen inside each training fold (expanding season split, no peeking at the scored season). Chosen C is logged on each child run and in the fold table. Tags are `phase=2` and `hypothesis=ridge-reference`. The report is `reports/phase2_ridge/`. If `logistic_l2` `h2_full` is not worse, it becomes the next reference. See `docs/experiments/phase2_ridge_reference.md`.
- Accept a phase 2 set only when pooled log loss improves by at least 0.003 and the 95% interval lies entirely below 0.
- A `--cv` invocation logs one parent run and one nested child per scored model. The parent holds `comparison.md`, `comparison.csv`, `best_feature_set`, and `data_digest`. Each child logs `decision` (`accepted`, `rejected`, `reference`, `baseline`, or `inconclusive`) and `log_loss_diff`, `log_loss_diff_ci_low`, `log_loss_diff_ci_high`. The same `data_digest` on the parent and the children means they used the same matrix. In the MLflow UI, filter with `tags.decision` and compare the child runs.
- Log sklearn models with the reviewed skops trusted-types allowlist only (`REVIEWED_SKOPS_TRUSTED_TYPES`). An unknown type fails closed.
- `reports/` at the repo root is gitignored local scratch (`reports/phase0/`, `reports/phase1/`, `reports/phase2/`, `reports/phase2_h2/`, `reports/phase2_h3/`, `reports/phase2_ridge/`, `reports/epa_filter_check.md`). Do not commit it.
- `docs/experiments/reports/` holds frozen snapshots. Add or replace one only when that hypothesis is decided. Do not hand-edit the numbers. Phase 0 and Phase 1 snapshots are not there yet. Link each experiment note to its snapshot. The index is `docs/experiments/reports/README.md`.
